      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Tower of Rot [zone=999]\n**Who:**\n- Deidre Harath [npc=47047]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Pile of Rot [item=116812]\n- Quincy's Bloodstone Detector [item=116888]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Adana Baxter [npc=47143]\n- Lieutenant Caridi [npc=47145]\n- Quincy Hollows [ _General Supplies_]\n- a Scion deathmask [npc=47140]\n- a Scion harrier [npc=47141]\n- a Scion thrasher [npc=47142]\n- a bubonian thrall [npc=47135]\n- an injured Scion [npc=47068]\n**Related Quests:**\n- A Rotten Heart [quest=7537]\n- Raid Expedition: Lord Kyle Bayle [quest=7539]\n- The Fall of Lord Bayle [quest=7538]\n- Tower of Rot #1: The Scions of the Tower [quest=7531]\n- Tower of Rot #2: The Tower's Victims [quest=7532]\n- Tower of Rot #3: Fenn's Job [quest=7533]\n- Tower of Rot #4: Narius' Plan [quest=7534]\n- Tower of Rot #6: The Source of Rot [quest=7536]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed May 21 07:01:17 2014\nModified: Sun Sep 22 16:13:22 2024 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task is the fifth in a series of six. It begins with Deidre Harath ( **click for map image**) on the zone-in level of the Tower of Rot._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Completed \"The Scions of the Tower\"\n\\- Completed \"The Tower's Victims\"\n\\- Completed \"Fenn's Job\"\n\\- Completed \"Narius' Plan\"\n_Say \"prevent\" to request the task._\nYou say, 'Hail, Deidre Harath'\nDeidre Harath smashes a fist into her hand. '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, this is not going as well as I had hoped! You have done well, though; don't mistake my anger. It's Adana with whom I am angry. While you attempted to descry Narius' plan, Adana swept through here with a band of Scions and stirred up [mayhem].\nYou say, 'Mayhem?'\nDeidre Harath says 'Three of our own were killed, and six wounded. Adana also destroyed a fair portion of Quincy's supplies, including a week's worth of rations. Until we can [secure] our position, stopping Narius will be impossible.'\nYou say, 'How can we secure it?'\nDeidre Harath says 'Quincy is taking stock of what supplies he has left. He also lived through the brunt of the attack. As we put the camp in order, I need you to seek Adana and [prevent] her from returning to finish what she started.'\nYou say, 'I'll prevent her from it'\nDeidre Harath says 'Once again, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, we would be lost without you. Speak with Quincy Hollows first. He might have an idea where Adana was headed.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Adana Problem'.\nAdana Baxter and a Scion raiding party have attacked Deidre's position and destroyed some of Quincy's supplies. Now you must retaliate and ensure this doesn't happen again.\n\n---\n\n**Summary**\n\\- Hail Quincy to receive \"Quincy's Bloodstone Detector\".\n\\- Right-click the \"Quincy's Bloodstone Detector\" to receive directional emotes to an update location.\n\\-\\-\\- Tells you above or below; direction (north, west, etc.); and how many paces away.\n_Note: If you have multiple people in your group on the same ambush step, ambush mobs will continue spawning at their timed intervals until you've gotten all kill credits. If, on the first ambush step, for example, you're DPS'ing the second thrall spawn and the 60-second timer passes before it dies, a third thrall will spawn. (You may be able to avoid multiple spawns by moving away from the trigger point, killing the spawned mobs, and then returning to the trigger point to spawn more.)_\n\\- Ambush area #1: One floor above the zone-in (bandits/grave robbers level):\n\\- Step over the update location (may be fixed or random - not confirmed) to trigger ambush spawns.\n\\-\\-\\- 3x \"a bubonian thrall\" auto-aggro spawns (staggered, separated by about 60 seconds).\n\\- Ambush area #2: Two floors above the zone-in (gnolls level):\n\\- Step over the update location (may be fixed or random - not confirmed) to trigger ambush spawns.\n\\-\\-\\- 4x \"a Scion harrier\" auto-aggro spawns (staggered in waves of two, separated by 105 seconds).\n\\- Ambush area #3: Four floors above the zone-in (undead level):\n\\- Step over the update location (may be fixed or random - not confirmed) to trigger ambush spawns.\n\\-\\-\\- 4x \"a Scion thrasher\" auto-aggro spawns (staggered in waves of two, separated by 150 seconds).\n\\-\\-\\- Once thrashers are dead, you have another set to deal with: 4x \"a Scion deathmask\" (has same spawning mechanism).\n\\- Hail \"an injured Scion\".\n\\- Move down one floor and spawn Lieutenant Caridi in the western room of the floor.\n\\- Say \"Adana\" to him to make him aggro; then kill him.\n\\- Head to the northern room of this same floor to spawn Adana Baxter.\n\\- Say \"ploy\" to make her aggro; DPS her to low health for the update.\n\\- Hail Quincy, then deliver 3x \"Pile of Rot\" to him.\n\\- Hail Deidre to complete.\n\n---\n\n**Map**\n!\n\n---\n\n02. Speak with Quincy Hollows 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak with Quincy Hollows and find out what happened when the Scions attacked.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Quincy Hollows'\n\n\n\n\nQuincy Hollows says 'Oh, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, it was just terrible... terrible! That cruel woman and her Scions crept out of the shadows while we were asleep and started slaughtering us and destroying my wares. If my guards hadn't been on duty we'd all be dead! As we began to rally, Adana and her band fled up the stairwell. It looked like one of her companions was pricked by our swords, since she left drops of blood behind. And that will be their [undoing]!'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Their undoing?'\n\n\n\n\nQuincy Hollows says 'I found this stone in one of my crates. I don't remember where I picked it up... probably from one of my bulk deals buying pirate plunder sight unseen. It vibrates in the presence of blood and should help you follow the trail of that injured Scion. Go get them for us, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! I always settle my debts, so you'll be the agent of my payback!'\n\n\n\n\n_You receive \"Quincy's Bloodstone Detector\". This item, when right-clicked, tells you where to go to get the next seven updates (will tell you to go above, below, or somewhere on your level; a direction; and how far away a location update is)._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n03. Follow the Scion raiding party's blood trail 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n04. Deal with any Scions or thralls you find 0/3 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Use Quincy's Bloodstone Detector to follow the trail of Scion blood and find out where the raiding party went. Deal with any threats you discover.\n\n\n\n\n_When you right-click the Detector, you'll see an emote like this (right-clicking has a cast time and breaks invis):_\n\n\n\nYou detect a concentration of blood above your location, to the east, at approximately 123 paces away.\n\n\n\n\n_Head to the direction indicated (click effect has unlimited charges). Upon entering the update area for this step, you'll see an emote:_\n\n\n\nYou feel the presence of Scion raiders.\n\n\n\n\n_Soon after this emote (30 seconds or so), 1x \"a bubonian thrall\" spawns and attacks (auto-aggro). 60 seconds later, another one spawns. The thralls hit for a max ~13,000._\n\n\n\n_Note: Update locations may also be visually indicated by a trail of blood drops on the ground. It's not known for sure whether the ambush update locations are fixed (the same locations every time), or if they're randomized._\n\n\n\n_Warning: If you have multiple people in your group on the same ambush step, ambush mobs will continue spawning at their timed intervals until you've gotten all kill credits. If, on the first ambush step, for example, you're DPS'ing the second thrall spawn and the 60-second timer passes before it dies, a third thrall will spawn. (You may be able to avoid multiple spawns by moving away from the trigger point, killing the spawned mobs, and then returning to the trigger point to spawn more.)_\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n05. The trail leads higher. Follow the Scions. 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n06. Deal with any Scions you find 0/4 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Continue using Quincy's Bloodstone Detector to follow the Scion trail. Deal with any threats you discover.\n\n\n\n\n_Same as above, except you get 2x \"a Scion harrier\" at a time (waves separated by 105 seconds), for four total. These hit for a max ~14,000._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n07. Discover the end of the blood trail 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n08. Prepare for any treachery 0/4 (Tower of Rot)\n\n09. Deal the final blows to the Scion raiders 0/4 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Quincy's Bloodstone Detector indicates the blood trail climbs still higher into the tower. Be prepared to face any Scion threats that you find.\n\n\n\n\n_Same as above two encounters, except you get 2x \"a Scion thrasher\", followed by 2x \"a Scion thrasher\" 2.5 minutes later. Once the thrashers are dead, another set of mobs will spawn: 2x \"a Scion deathmask\" followed by 2x \"a Scion deathmask\" (waves separated by 2.5 minutes). Each of these mobs hit for a max ~14,000._\n\n\n\n_Warning: Keep in mind that if you have multiple people in group at this step, waves of mobs will continue spawning every 2.5 minutes until everyone has the task updated. (You may be able to avoid multiple spawns by moving away from the trigger point, killing the spawned mobs, and then returning to the trigger point to spawn more.)_\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n10. Examine the scene 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Hail \"an injured Scion\"._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, an injured Scion'\n\n\n\n\nan injured Scion says 'Welcome to your death, fools! The poison now flows within you! Best start eating any piles of rot you can find, or face a swift death. If Lieutenant Caridi hadn't gone to the floor below, he'd laugh at how well Adana's plan has worked. ' The injured Scion coughs into her hand and slumps to the floor. 'If only I could be there... To laugh when you breathed your last...'\n\n\n\n\nThe injured Scion's blade has punctured your side and injected poison into your veins. You feel weakness spreading through your body.\n\n\n\n\n_You become poisoned with \"Mild Bone Rot\" (limits hitpoints to 80%), which you'll have to deal with for now._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n11. Find Lieutenant Caridi 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n12. Confront Lieutenant Caridi 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ You have been poisoned by the injured Scion. You must consume Piles of Rot from the ground in order to prevent the poison from killing you. Before the Scion died, she mentioned that Lieutenant Caridi had gone to the floor below. Seek him out and confront him.\n\n\n\n\n_Optional: You can temporarily cure the poison buff on you by using one of the green ground spawns (\"Pile of Rot\") scattered around the floor. This stops the effects for 35-40 seconds._\n\n\n\n_Head to /loc 15, 120, 302 to spawn Lieutenant Caridi and say \"Adana\" to make him aggro:_\n\n\n\nYou sense Lieutenant Caridi is nearby.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Lieutenant Caridi'\n\n\n\n\nLieutenant Caridi laughs and shoulders his club. 'Walked right into it, didn't ya? Feel it hot in yer belly, like a slug of drink? That's the rot, and yer done for! There'll be nothin' left for [Adana] to kill. She'll be so sad!\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Adana?'\n\n\n\n\nLieutenant Caridi says 'Oh, she had business elsewhere on this floor, but ya got nothin' to worry about. Yer never gonna see her again anyway. She said if I see you I'm to bust yer head open, so that's what I'm gonna do!'\n\n\n\n\n_After a short delay, he goes aggro. He hits for a max ~17,500; has ~8.5 million hitpoints; and casts \"Club to the Head\" on random targets (nuke for 40,000 dmg + spinstun)._\n\n\n\nLieutenant Caridi has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n13. Find Adana Baxter 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n14. Confront Adana Baxter 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ The poison within you is intensifying. You must confront Adana Baxter on the floor where you fought Caridi if you wish to learn the truth.\n\n\n\n\n_While on this portion of the task, you are inflicted with \"Moderate Bone Rot\" (limits hitpoints to 70%). Again, this can be temporarily (optionally) cured by using the \"Pile of Rot\" items (green ground spawns) scattered throughout the floor._\n\n\n\n_Head to /loc 90, 60, 306 to spawn Adana Baxter. Now, you get inflicted with \"Severe Bone Rot\" (reduction in hitpoints by 65%):_\n\n\n\nYou hear Adana laughing nearby.\n\n\n\n\nAs you approach Adana, the rot intensifies and seeps into your bones.\n\n\nYou feel yourself rotting from the inside out.\n\n\n\n\n_Hail her, and follow her dialogue, saying \"ploy\" to her to make her aggro:_\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Adana Baxter'\n\n\n\n\nAdana Baxter smiles at you. 'Why, is that my old friend, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_? So wonderful to see you! And are you well? Oh, my, you don't look so well! Are you ill? Have you eaten something foul? Or did one of my little drones sting you? You really are too [trusting], always believing whatever apparent truth is thrust in front of you!\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Trusting?'\n\n\n\n\nAdana Baxter says 'There are more important things in this world than friendship, loyalty, or honor -- things like the power to control life and death. I once thought you would be the one to kill Kyle Bayle and make my path clear, but obviously Narius is more capable than you are. You can't even recognize an obvious [ploy]!'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'What ploy?'\n\n\n\n\nAdana Baxter says 'Quincy's guards didn't cut my little Scion drone. My blades are sharper than that merchant's will ever be. The only surprise is that you've lived this long, despite ambushes and a gut full of rot. By now your bones should be turning to gruel, and you are of no more use than a pot of spoiled porridge. I think it's time we ended our working relationship.'\n\n\n\n\n_Ater a short delay, she goes aggro. She has ~8.5 million hitpoints; and casts \"Break Brittle Bones\" on random targets (nuke for 46,000 dmg). DPS her to 10% for the update._\n\n\n\nAdana Baxter steps back, laughing. 'Quite tenacious! But don't start thinking I'll regret choosing Narius over you. A tenacious fool is still a fool, and an honorable corpse is still dead. I don't have time to trifle further with the doomed; Narius is about to enter the source of rot, so I must be off. Enjoy your last few minutes before the rot consumes you!' Adana Baxter disappears into the shadows.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n15. Speak with Quincy to find a cure 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Tell Quincy Hollows what has happened. Perhaps he can make a cure for you using several Piles of Rot.\n\n\n\n\n_Remove any \"Pile of Rot\" items from your inventory, and hail Quincy Hollows. You'll need to bring him 3x \"Pile of Rot\" (if you had some on you, they don't count) and hail him again._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Quincy Hollows'\n\n\n\n\nQuincy Hollows says '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, you look awful! Do you have three handfuls of those rot piles you found? I think I have an elixir that might bind with the rot and be able to purge it once and for all from your body.'\n\n\n\n\n_With 3x \"Pile of Rot\" in your inventory, hail him again:_\n\n\n\nQuincy Hollows takes three piles of rot from you and drops them into an elixir. As the concoction bubbles and smokes, you drink it down and feel strength creeping back into your body. 'You're looking better already! I think the worst of the malady has passed, but I would take it easy. Oh, I hope those horrible raiders don't return with poisoned blades for the lot of us! How will I ever have enough elixirs?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n16. Speak with Deidre Harath 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Quincy has cured you. Tell Deidre Harath all that has passed.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Deidre Harath'\n\n\n\n\nDeidre Harath says 'So Adana still lives... At least you put an end to her fellow raiders. You look a bit worse off for your efforts, but I still must ask you for yet another sacrifice. Narius is entering the source of rot and must be stopped. With our camp secured, now is the time.'\n\n\n\n\nYou have killed Adana Baxter's raiding party, although Adana herself escaped. Now she and Narius are about to enter the source of rot.\n\n---\n\n_Rewards:_\n300 platinum\nExperience (about 3% in Level 100)",
