      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Tower of Rot [zone=999]\n**Who:**\n- Deidre Harath [npc=47047]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Empowered Magelock Stone [item=117028]\n- Magelock Fragment [item=116904]\n- Magelock Stone [item=116909]\n- Raw Mana Flask [item=116903]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Brendaleen Thundershield [npc=47048]\n- Guard Werben [npc=47061]\n- Quincy Hollows [ _General Supplies_]\n- Ritualist Farji [npc=47147]\n- a captured apprentice [npc=47069]\n- a cowering apprentice [npc=47072]\n- a defender of rot [npc=47137]\n- first altar of rot [npc=47065]\n- second altar of rot [npc=47066]\n- third altar of rot [npc=47067]\n**Related Quests:**\n- A Rotten Heart [quest=7537]\n- Raid Expedition: Lord Kyle Bayle [quest=7539]\n- The Fall of Lord Bayle [quest=7538]\n- Tower of Rot #1: The Scions of the Tower [quest=7531]\n- Tower of Rot #2: The Tower's Victims [quest=7532]\n- Tower of Rot #3: Fenn's Job [quest=7533]\n- Tower of Rot #4: Narius' Plan [quest=7534]\n- Tower of Rot #5: The Adana Problem [quest=7535]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed May 21 07:01:35 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This solo task is the final task in a series of six. It begins with Dedire Harath ( **click for map image**) on the zone-in level of the Tower of Rot._\n_Pre-Requisites:_\n\\- Completed \"The Scions of the Tower\"\n\\- Completed \"The Tower's Victims\"\n\\- Completed \"Fenn's Job\"\n\\- Completed \"Narius' Plan\"\n\\- Completed \"The Adana Problem\"\n\n---\n\n**Summary & Requesting the Task**\n_Say \"open it\" to request the task._\n\\- Hail Brendaleen.\n\\- Hail \"a captured apprentice\" (two floors below zone-in).\n\\- Location update in the southern room of the basement to spawn Ritualist Farji.\n\\- Kill Ritualist Farji, and loot the \"Raw Mana Flask\" from his corpse (drops one per kill).\n\\- Hail Brendaleen.\n\\- Hail Guard Werben (top floor).\n\\- Kill \"a cowering apprentice\" until you've looted 8x \"Magelock Fragment\".\n\\- Hail Quincy Hollows.\n\\- Use the jewelry table next to him to craft a \"Magelock Stone\" (combine the flask + 8 fragments).\n\\- DPS ghost mobs to under 20% health and click the stone on them (repeat x10 to get \"Empowered Magelock Stone\").\n\\- Head to the bottom floor and use the Magelock Stone on an altar to make it damageable, then kill it.\n\\-\\-\\- 1-2x \"a defender of rot\" (200k hp; AEs a 27k nuke) every 20 seconds while the altar is engaged.\n\\-\\-\\- Do this for each of the three altars in the basement.\n\\- Hail Deidre to complete.\nYou say, 'Hail, Deidre Harath'\nDeidre Harath says 'Glad you are still with us. I've been convinced so far that nothing can kill you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, but that seemed a little too close. In good news, Brendaleen confirmed that Narius has locked himself in the lowest chambers. We think Fenn and Adana are both there. This is our chance to launch an attack, but Narius or his people have sealed the door with a magical lock. Getting past it is beyond my knowledge. Can you [open it]?'\nYou say, 'Of course, I'll open it'\nDeidre Harath says 'Brendaleen might just have an answer for us. One of her scouts caught a Scion apprentice and has learned more about the seal Narius has placed on the source of rot. You should assist Brendaleen in breaking the seal.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Source of Rot'.\nNarius has sealed himself within the source of rot, and Deidre needs you to find a way inside.\n\n---\n\n**Map**\n!\n\n---\n\n03. Speak with Brendaleen Thundershield 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ One of Brendaleen's scouts has caught a Scion apprentice that has knowledge of the magic used to seal the source of rot. Speak with Brendaleen.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Brendaleen Thundershield'\n\n\n\n\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'You know, I think I'm getting to like this spy business, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! It's like treasure hunting for secrets. And when I think about it, with the right buyer, [secrets] fetch more than gold...'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Secrets?'\n\n\n\n\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'Yes, I was getting to that! My lovely little spy, Jrint, turned up some interesting treasure. He followed one of the Scions' ritualist apprentices, and my guard scooped her up when she fell behind the procession of Scions that recently ascended the stairwell. The guard is holding her on the second floor of the basement.'\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n04. Speak with the apprentice that was captured on the second floor of the basement 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ To learn more about the sealing ritual, speak with the ritualist apprentice that was captured and is being held on the second floor of the basement.\n\n\n\n\n_Find \"a captured apprentice\" at /loc -5, 65, -397, and hail her._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a captured apprentice'\n\n\n\n\na captured apprentice says 'You're not going to hurt me, right? I told you all I know! Ritualist Farji sealed the entrance to the source with the altars of rot and the Magelock Stone. There's no getting in there as long as those altars remain, and you can't destroy them without using the fully powered Magelock Stone -- and it shattered after Farji used it, and he would never let you have the raw mana to power it -- and you're not going to kill me, right?'\n\n\n\n\na guard says 'I've heard enough of her whining! She's told us all that's useful!'\n\n\n\n\na captured apprentice died.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n05. Find the entrance to source of rot on the lowest level of the basement 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n06. Confront Ritualist Farji and take the Raw Mana Flask from him 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ You must find Ritualist Farji near the entrance to source of rot, on the lowest level of the basement. Confront him and take the Raw Mana Flask from him by any means.\n\n\n\n\n_Head to the basement level, /loc -155, -20, -496, to spawn Ritualist Farji:_\n\n\n\nYou sense the presence of Ritualist Farji.\n\n\n\n\n_Follow his dialogue, saying \"Magelock Stone\" to him to make him aggro:_\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Ritualist Farji'\n\n\n\n\nRitualist Farji says 'Oh, ho! You think to follow the master? What courage you have! It's so amusing when braggarts think their courage more powerful than my [rituals]!'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Rituals?'\n\n\n\n\nRitualist Farji says 'The door is sealed, the key shattered. My apprentices have seen to that. By the looks of your coarse hands and atavistic face, you wouldn't be able to mend a torn sleeve let alone the [Magelock Stone]!'\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'What is the Magelock Stone?'\n\n\n\n\nRitualist Farji says 'Its description would be too much for your simple mind to comprehend. I will not explain its power to bind or release defenses. The only explanations fit for creatures such as you are spoken in the language of brutal violence!'\n\n\n\n\n_After a short delay, he goes aggro. He hits for a max ~23,000 (no flurry; no rampage) and has an emote-based AE \"Mana Pulse\" (50' range nuke for 45k + 10k mana drain -- 15-to-20 second delay between emote and cast):_\n\n\n\nRitualist Farji prepares to expel a mana pulse.\n\n\nRitualist Farji expels a mana pulse.\n\n\n\n\n_Kill him and loot \"Raw Mana Flask\" from his corpse._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n07. Speak with Brendaleen Thundershield 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that you have learned more about the seal and the Magelock Stone, speak with Brendaleen and see what she thinks.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Brendaleen Thundershield'\n\n\n\n\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'A Magelock Stone and a mana flask? Tresures? Now you're speaking my language! When you're done with these, don't forget your friend Brendaleen! Now, if you're after apprentices, I think those Scions that ascended the stairwell earlier had a green look about them. I sent Guard Werben to follow them after we snatched the straggler. Get up there and talk to Werben; he should know by now what the Scions are planning.'\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n08. Speak with Guard Werben 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Guard Werben has been following the apprentices that might be carrying fragments of the Magelock Stone. Speak to Werben on the highest floor of the tower.\n\n\n\n\n_Guard Werben is found on the top floor at /loc -55, -30, 503._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Werben'\n\n\n\n\nGuard Werben says 'Quiet! You don't want to spook the apprentices! They're scared enough as it is. They're trembling at the sight of all these malevolent spirits here, and I don't blame them! From what I've heard, they were sent with some stone fragments to try to perform some rituals to clear the way to Kyle Bayle. But they've been too afraid to do their duty. Cowards!'\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n09. Kill the cowering apprentices and recover the Magelock Fragments 0/8 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ The apprentices are trying to gain access to Kyle Bayle's sanctum. Kill the cowering apprentices and retrieve the Magelock Fragments from them.\n\n\n\n\n_Kill \"a cowering apprentice\" mobs on the top floor of the tower until you've looted 8x \"Magelock Fragment\". As far as DPS goes, these mobs are average difficulty (mezzable; hit for a max ~17,500). It's been reported they may be highly resistant to magic-based spells._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n\nSpeak with Quincy Hollows 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Quincy Hollows might know how to repair the Magelock Stone. Speak with him.\n\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Quincy Hollows'\n\n\n\n\nQuincy Hollows looks over the fragments of stone and the mana flask. 'I'm not an expert on magical stones, but I'd say you would need a jeweler's skill to repair such an intricate object. Perhaps combining the mana flask with the fragments would help fuse the stone together?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n10. Repair the Magelock Stone using a jewelry crafting table 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Quincy thinks you can repair the Magelock Stone using a jewel crafting table, the Magelock Fragments, and the Raw Mana Flask.\n\n\n\n\n_There is a jewelry crafting table near Quincy Hollows (/loc -135, 50, 4). In it, combine 8x \"Magelock Fragment\" + 1x \"Raw Mana Flask\" to produce 1x \"Magelock Stone\"._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n\nSpeak with Quincy Hollows 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Quincy Hollows'\n\n\n\n\nQuincy Hollows holds the repaired Magelock Stone and frowns. 'It still looks... dead. I think it needs some sort of power. I've traded a few trinkets like this before, and the sellers -- always frightening, threatening-looking folks -- told me such objects could be powered by souls and spirits. There are plenty of ghosts at the top of the tower, right? Perhaps they could bring life back to the stone!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n11. Weaken the spirits haunting the tower and capture them with the Magelock Stone 0/10 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ You need to charge the Magelock Stone in order to use it. Quincy thinks you should weaken the ghosts in the tower and use the stone to absorb their spirits.\n\n\n\n\n_DPS ghost mobs to low health (under 20%) and right-click the Magelock Stone (this is an instant kill of the mob). Repeat until this step updates and you receive \"Empowered Magelock Stone\". Note that if you're doing this as a group, a single click will update your entire group._\n\n\n\na pine protector's spirit is captured in the Magelock Stone.\n\n\na pine protector's energy is absorbed into the Magelock.\n\n\na pine protector's corpse is silent and still.\n\n\na pine protector died.\n\n\n\n\n_Upon the last click, you'll see:_\n\n\n\nYou have successfully powered the Magelock Stone!\n\n\n\n\n_You receive \"Empowered Magelock Stone\" on your cursor._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n12. Destroy the first altar of rot on the lowest level of the basement 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n13. Destroy the second altar of rot on the lowest level of the basement 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n14. Destroy the third altar of rot on the lowest level of the basement 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Now that the Magelock Stone has been charged, use it to make the altars of rot vulnerable and destroy them.\n\n\n\n\n_Altar locations:_\n\n\n\nFirst: -155, 40, -496\n\n\nSecond: 85, 65, -497\n\n\nThird: 130, -50, -496\n\n\n\n\n_Use the \"Empowered Magelock Stone\" on an altar to make it damageable (remains damageable for two minutes, after which you have to click again):_\n\n\n\nthird altar of rot's defenses are weakened by the Magelock.\n\n\nThird altar of rot's defenses are destroyed.\n\n\n\n\nthird altar of rot regains its defenses.\n\n\n\n\n_For every 20 seconds an altar is vulnerable to damage, adds spawn on top of it: 1x \"a defender of rot\" up to around 30% health, and then 2x \"a defender of rot\" to the altar's 'death'. These adds have about 200,000 hp in health; hit for a max ~5,500; and cast a 25' range PBAE called \"Skeleslash\":_\n\n\n\nSkeleslash: PB AE 25', Disease (-975)\n\n\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 27692\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n15. Speak with Deidre Harath 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Deidre Harath'\n\n\n\n\nDeidre Harath says 'The way has been opened? No doubt many sacrifices were made to do so. Now we must strike!'\n\n\n\n\nYou have successfully destroyed the magical barrier that sealed the source of rot. You can now prepare to confront Narius.\n\n_Rewards:_\n412 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (about 4% in Level 100)",
