      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Tower of Rot [zone=999]\n**Who:**\n- Brendaleen Thundershield [npc=47048]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 65\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 03:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Pulsing Phase Crystal [item=117217]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Tower of Rot: Brendaleen's Scheme [zone=1003]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Brendaleen Thundershield [npc=47172]\n- Commander Meredith [npc=47173]\n- Guardian Roger Macholeth [npc=47058]\n- Macholeth`s squire Salria [npc=47174]\n- a bandit - Tower of Rot - 2 [npc=47149]\n- a bloated devourer [npc=47150]\n- a brigand [npc=47151]\n- a bubonian guardian [npc=47152]\n- a bubonian scavenger [npc=47153]\n- a caustic muck [npc=47154]\n- a decaying sporemound [npc=47155]\n- a famished feeder [npc=47156]\n- a frenzied gnoll [npc=47157]\n- a furious miner [npc=47158]\n- a gnoll guardsman - Tower of Rot [npc=47159]\n- a gnoll oracle [npc=47160]\n- a gnoll runt [npc=47161]\n- a grave robber [npc=47162]\n- a noxious deathcap [npc=47163]\n- a rockbreaker [npc=47164]\n- a rotting sporemound [npc=47165]\n- a stoneshell pest [npc=47166]\n- a tomb raider [npc=47167]\n- a tower scion [npc=47168]\n- an archaic trilobite [npc=47169]\n- an excavator [npc=47171]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Daily Task: Heroic Adventures [quest=7988]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed May 21 07:07:01 2014\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n**About Heroic Adventures**\n\\- The Tower of Rot heroic adventure scales as low as **Level 65** and up to current maximum level.\n\\- Scale is based on the highest level player **present in the zone** and affects difficulty, loot quality, and mob levels.\n\\- There is some variation/randomization in the task steps you'll be assigned as you progress through the task.\n\\- Time of completion will vary by your group's makeup (anywhere from 30-90+ minutes).\n\\- Collection items appear as ground spawns midway through tasks (you'll see an emote indicating their appearance).\n\\- Named mobs (or their PHs) spawn midway through tasks (usually, but always, at the same time collection items appear).\n\\- These tasks have individual **3-hour lockout timers** (timer gained upon completion).\n**Experience in Heroic Adventures**\n\\- Mobs in these instances grant some experience, but the bulk of experience is **earned upon task completion**.\n\\- As of a patch in November 2014, less difficult tasks were tuned to reward less experience and more difficult ones were tuned to reward more.\n\\- For an added experience bonus, check out **Guard Hamarn's \"Daily Tasks\"** [quest=7988].\n\n---\n\n_This is a heroic adventure (1-6 players) that begins with Brendaleen Thundershield ( **click for map image**) on the zone-in level of the Tower of Rot._\n_Pre-Requisites for Requesting:_\n\\- Level 65\n\\- No tasks\n\n---\n\n**TASK SUMMARY**\n\\- Say \"yes\" to request the task and \"ready\" to zone in.\n**Step #1:**\n\\- Speak to Brendaleen 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail update.\n**Step #2:**\n\\- Recover a Pulsing Phase Crystal from bandits or brigands within the tower 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill bandits and brigands until you've looted the crystal.\n\\- Recover a Pulsing Phase Crystal from tomb raiders or grave robbers within the tower 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill tomb raiders and grave robbers until you've looted the crystal.\n**Step #3:**\n\\- Clear a path to the portal 0/15\n\\-\\-\\- Kill gnolls and stoneshell pests between the stairwell and the portal.\n\\- Clear a path to the portal 0/13\n\\-\\-\\- Kill miners, undead, and mucks between the stairwell and the portal.\n\\- Clear a path to the portal 0/12\n\\-\\-\\- Kill mucks and sporalis between the stairwell and the portal.\n\\- Clear a path to the portal 0/14\n\\-\\-\\- Kill trilobites, bubonians, and devourers between the stairwell and the portal.\n**\\- At this point in the task, a named (or its PH) has a chance to spawn, and collectibles for Unnatural Life [quest=7570] spawn.**\n**Step #4:**\n\\- Defeat the tower scions guarding the portal 0/2\n\\-\\-\\- Kill 2x \"a tower scion\".\n**Step #5:**\n\\- Use the Pulsing Phase Crystal to close the portal 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- This spawns a mob.\n**Step #6:**\n\\- Defeat the attacker that ambushed you! 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Kill the mob that spawned.\n**Step #7:**\n\\- Return to Brenadleen 0/1\n\\-\\-\\- Hail/Dialogue update.\n\\- As soon as the objective for Step #7 is done, the task completes.\n\n---\n\n**NAMED MOBS**\n_\"Guardian Roger Macholeth\" (or its PH \"Macholeth`s squire Salria\") has a chance to spawn on the bandit/brigand/grave robber/tomb raider level (one above the zone-in point) after the third step is completed. This emote signals his spawn:_\nThe bandits and tomb raiders cause a commotion as Guardian Roger Macholeth appears within the tower.\n_Known loot from this named:_\nMallard Mask\nMana Goggles\nSerrated Limb Lopper\n\n---\n\n**TASK IN DETAIL**\n========================================================================\nTRIGGERING THE TASK\n========================================================================\nYou say, 'Hail, Brendaleen Thundershield'\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'Take a look around you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. To a pessimist, this tower may present as a hopeless deathtrap, but as an opportunist, I see gold glittering in these rotting walls. Untold [treasures] lie in the rubble, just waiting to be claimed.'\nYou say, 'What treasures?'\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'Rather than despair at my unfortunate situation, I've spent my time scavenging, collecting a variety of artifacts and other curios. Some say it's a fool's errand, swearing that I'll live out my days, trapped in this tower, but I don't plan to die within these walls. In fact, I think I may have found a [trinket] that can help me escape with all my treasure!'\nYou say, 'What trinket?'\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'I found a crystal at the bottom of the tower, buried beneath some rubble. Under all the dirt and grime, it radiated the same eerie color that emanates from the portals. It must have been important, because as soon as I got my hands on it, the tower scions rushed me. I escaped with my life, but the crystal was [lost] along the way.'\nYou say, 'Lost?'\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'I imagine a bandit or raider has their thieving hands on it by now. They couldn't possibly know the true value of the crystal. We need to recover it, and use it to close the portals. Without the constant influx of creatures, I may be able to make a run for it and escape with my treasure, leaving some behind for you of course! So will you help me, [yes] or [no]?'\nYou say, 'No, I'm not going to help you! Do it yourself'\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'What, you don't like treasure?' The dwarf rolls her eyes and sighs, 'Well, if you won't do it for me, then do it for all the helpless victims trapped within this tower. If those portals remain active, they'll never be able to escape. Surely you can say [yes] to helping them.''\nYou say, 'Yes, fine, OK!'\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'That's the spirit!' The treasure hunter lowers her voice, 'Let's go somewhere a little more private to discuss the details. Let me know when you're [ready] and I'll meet you near the stairwell.''\nYou have been assigned the task 'Brendaleen's Scheme'.\nHelp Brendleen close the portals within the Tower of Rot so that others may escape.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Tower of Rot.\n========================================================================\nSTEP #1\n========================================================================\nSpeak to Brendaleen 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Speak to Brendaleen once you've moved to a more private location.\n_If You Get This Step: Hail her._\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'Grave robbers and bandits roam the floor above. After you've reacquired the crystal from the thieves, clear a path to one of the portals. When the route from the portal to the stairwell is clear, use the crystal and keep your fingers crossed. With any luck, the portal will close. I'll stay here, guarding our treasure. Good luck!'\n========================================================================\nSTEP #2\n========================================================================\nRecover a Pulsing Phase Crystal from bandits or brigands within the tower 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Recover the pulsing crystal from bandits or brigands a couple floors above Brendaleen.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill bandits and brigands until you loot a \"Pulsing Phase Crystal\"._\n=====================\nRecover a Pulsing Phase Crystal from tomb raiders or grave robbers within the tower 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Recover the pulsing crystal from grave robbers or tomb raiders a couple floors above Brendaleen.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill tomb raiders and grave robbers until you loot a \"Pulsing Phase Crystal\"._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #3\n========================================================================\nClear a path to the portal 0/15 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Once you've located the portal, create an escape route by killing all creatures between the portal and the stairwell.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill gnolls and stoneshell pests between the stairwell and the portal._\n=====================\nClear a path to the portal 0/13 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Once you've located the portal, create an escape route by killing all creatures between the portal and the stairwell.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill miners, undead, and mucks between the stairwell and the portal._\n=====================\nClear a path to the portal 0/12 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Once you've located the portal, create an escape route by killing all creatures between the portal and the stairwell.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill mucks and sporalis between the stairwell and the portal._\n=====================\nClear a path to the portal 0/14 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Once you've located the portal, create an escape route by killing all creatures between the portal and the stairwell.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill trilobites, bubonians, and devourers between the stairwell and the portal._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #4\n========================================================================\nDefeat the tower scions guarding the portal 0/2 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ You must defeat the tower scions before attempting to close the portal.\n_If You Get This Step: Kill 2x \"a tower scion\"._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #5\n========================================================================\nUse the Pulsing Phase Crystal to close the portal 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ Stand near the active portal and use the Pulsing Phase Crystal.\n_If You Get This Step: Using the crystal near the portal will either close the portal and spawn Commander Meredith (aggro's), or will fail to close it and spawn \"a famished feeder\"._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #6\n========================================================================\nDefeat the attacker that ambushed you! 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Kill either \"a famished feaster\" or \"Commander Meredith\"._\n========================================================================\nSTEP #7\n========================================================================\nReturn to Brenadleen 0/1 (Tower of Rot)\n_Task Window Says:_ ?\n_If You Get This Step: Hail, dialogue to complete._\nBrendaleen Thundershield sighs with disappointment, \"So the portal didn't close? Well, I'm not ready to give up just yet. I'll have to acquire another crystal and try again. Let's [leave] this area for now and return to the safety of the main floor.'\n--or--\nBrendaleen Thundershield says 'Well done, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! With every portal closed, we get one step closer to having a safe escape route! Let's [leave] this area for now and return to the safety of the main floor.''\n\n---\n\n**TASK REWARDS**\n\\- a varying amount of platinum\n\\- a varying amount of experience\n\\- a varying number of Marks of Valor (currency used to buy group gear)\n- Mark of Valor [item=113459]",
